# Cell from playpick: mode=walk, boss=saved, spec=rogue:assassination,
# style=melee, size=10, difficulty=normal, view=844x390,touch, save=fresh.
#
# First rogue this job has ever played (no prior session touches any
# rogue spec) and first melee-style walk in raid/clear mode -- melee has
# only been used on a battleground hunter before (direction.md's 2026-09-24
# note). The target, saved (The One You Save), sits in `dream`, deep in the
# frostwing wing past the whole lower spire and the crossing -- on a fresh
# save this walk cannot skip THE VIGIL, and four separate runs this job has
# made (mash, auto in mode=walk; wander, good, flee in mode=clear) all
# either wiped there (#271, unretryable) or stalled at the same fixed point
# a dozen units apart (#6/#281). melee is the one style that stands and
# fights rather than running past or beelining through -- the README's own
# claim about the passage is that "standing at the door trading with
# whatever comes out... is the wrong answer; the answer is to walk into
# it," so this is close to the literal wrong answer, on purpose: does
# actively fighting the watchmen get further than avoiding them, die
# faster, or converge on the same spot anyway?
open
tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:rogue:assassination
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot arrive-threshold
state
targets

evening melee 200 10
shot after-evening
state
says
bill
